      "id": "fb-002",
      "question": "How are SIM bundles managed?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 21.09,
      "answer": "SIM bundles are managed through the SIM Cards module, which handles SIM inventory, telco relationships, APN profiles, data bundles, roaming, signal quality, and cost visibility. This module helps prevent surprise bills and silent outages, ensuring communication continuity for vehicles, people, cargo, generators, and remote equipment. It provides a complete SIM inventory showing ICCID, MSISDN, IMEI pairing, telco, tariff plan, current asset, status, and country, allowing for cost control and reduction of orphaned subscriptions.\n\nSource: OLIWA User Stories — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
