    {
      "id": "fb-006",
      "question": "What is VEBA escrow?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 28.56,
      "answer": "VEBA escrow is a system that holds a renter's payment in tokens when they book an asset. It releases the payment to the owner only once telematics data confirms that the asset was used as agreed. This includes verifying engine hours, geofence-confirmed possession, duration, and usage class.\n\nA booking moves through states such as reserved, active, and released. It can also become disputed, refunded, or partially adjusted if the usage doesn't match the booking.\n\nSource: NAVAS Ecosystem Vision Scope Document — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
